  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227,$\" while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is positive. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is irrational or integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{\u00a0is irrational}}_{\u23df}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{x\\text{\u00a0is integer}}_{\u23df}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q\u2228R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{\u00a0is positive}}_{\u23df}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{x\\text{\u00a0is irrational}\\text{\u00a0or integer}}_{\u23df}}_{Q\\,\u2228\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P\u2227(Q\u2228R).$",
